  ],
  "equipment_type": "Ducted split system BMS gateway",
  "applies_to": "ActronAir GW100K gateway connecting up to 10 ActronAir Advance, Aires, Classic Series 2 or VCC systems (each via an ICUNO-MOD card) to BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP.",
  "summary": "The GW100K translates the Modbus RTU data of up to ten ActronAir ICUNO-MOD cards to BACnet IP, BACnet MS/TP or Modbus TCP. Each system gets the same 121-point block (on/off, mode, setpoint, fan, economiser, zones, temperatures, compressor data, alarms, error codes); this list shows system 1 plus the 24 shared gateway I/O points (Device 11).",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Points are system (Device) 1 from the register table; systems 2-10 repeat the same 121 points with object names A2xx/D2xx/I2xx ... A10xx and their own instances (see sheets Device 2-10 in the XLSX).",
    "Instances do not follow one offset: from system 1 to system 2, writable AVs/IVs move +35 (some writable AVs +36), read-only AVs/IVs +42, writable BVs +27 and read-only BVs +23. The table also prints system 10's A1010 at instance 526, out of sequence.",
    "Device 11 points (A11xx, D11xx) are the gateway's own universal I/O and relays, shared by all systems.",
    "Points marked Advanced BMS mode only (A131, A132, D106) need the ICUNO-MOD in Advanced BMS mode (I110 shows the mode).",
    "Error codes (I116-I121) are listed in ActronAir document 9590-0000-05."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BMS Gateway Controller GW100K - BMS Register Table",
    "doc_number": "9590-3038-03 V1.0.1",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://actronair.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/9590-3038-03-BMS-Gateway-Register-Table.xlsx"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Turn the system on with D101, choose the mode with I103 and the setpoint with A101, and the fan with I101. Read room temperature, running capacity, compressor status and the alarm and error code points.",
